docker-compose up -d --build
# If you encounter issues with Docker build cache, you can clear it using the following commands:
Clear the Docker builder cache:
docker builder prune --all
Optionally, clear unused images and containers:
docker system prune --all
Re-run your Docker build command, possibly with the --no-cache flag:
docker-compose build --no-cache

docker compose up -d --build portfolio-frontend


To backup a MongoDb database, you can use the following script. Make sure to replace the placeholders with your actual MongoDB connection details and desired backup location.

chmod +x backup-mongo.sh
./backup-mongo.sh


Market-data service (Flask, port 5000) — Swagger UI for calling endpoints manually:

http://localhost:5000/apidocs        Swagger UI ("Try it out" on every endpoint)
http://localhost:5000/apispec.json   Raw OpenAPI spec

Endpoints:
POST /update/yahoo               Update market data via Yahoo Finance (body {"ticker": "AAPL"} = single; empty body = debounced batch over tickers queue)
POST /update/auto                Same, auto-routed by asset type (CRYPTO holding -> CoinGecko, else Yahoo)
POST /update/massive             Same, Massive API provider
POST /update/crypto              Same, CoinGecko provider (crypto tickers, e.g. BTC or BTC-USD; no API key)
POST /update/full                Full update for one ticker: market data + daily + monthly price history (body {"ticker": "AAPL"} required)
POST /update/sharesOutstanding   Backfill sharesOutstanding (body {"ticker": "AAPL"} = single; empty body = all marketData docs)
POST /update/exchangeRates       Fetch EUR FX rates from ECB
POST /history/refresh/<ticker>   Refresh daily price history for a ticker

Backend Swagger UI (Spring Boot): http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui.html